==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|əʊkə(r)|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{suffix|broke|er|lang=en}}.

====Adjective====
{{head|en|adjective comparative form}}

# {{en-comparative of|broke}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|broker|lang=enm}}, {{term|brokour|lang=enm}}, {{term|brocour|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{term|brocour||small trader|lang=fro}} (compare also {{term|abroker||to act as a broker|lang=fro}}), from {{etyl|odt|en}} {{m|odt|*brokere||one who determines the usages of trade, manager}}, from {{term|broke|lang=odt}}, {{term|bruyck|lang=odt}}, {{term|breuck||use, usage, trade|lang=odt}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*brūkiz||use, custom}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*bhrug-||to use, enjoy}}, equivalent to {{suffix|brook|er|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|brukere||a broker|lang=gml}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|bruger||a broker, user, handler|lang=da}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|bruk||use, custom, trade, business|lang=sv}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|broc||use, profit, advantage, foredeal|lang=ang}}. Compare also {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|brocanter||to deal in second-hand goods|lang=fr}} from the same Germanic source. More at {{l/en|brook}}.

====Noun====
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[mediator]] between a [[buyer]] and [[seller]].
# {{context|computing|lang=en}} An agent involved in the exchange of messages or transactions.

